{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# AgriLink: Machine Learning Recommendation Engine\n",
    "## Hybrid Matrix Factorization & Feature-Aware Recommendation Model\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook contains the complete **cell-by-cell execution** for AgriLink's crop recommendation engine.\n",
    "It processes user interactions (views, cart adds, purchases, ratings) alongside crop metadata (category, organic status, pricing) to produce personalized Top-10 crop listing recommendations for buyers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 1: Environment Setup & Library Imports\n",
    "Importing core data science and machine learning libraries: Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, SciPy, and Joblib."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "from scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Cell 1 Completed: All ML libraries imported successfully!')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 2: Data Ingestion (Supabase & Excel Database)\n",
    "Loading dummy datasets for Users, Crop Listings, and User Interactions from `AgriLink_Dummy_Database.xlsx`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "excel_path = os.path.join('..', 'agrilink-database', 'AgriLink_Dummy_Database.xlsx')\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(excel_path):\n",
    "    excel_path = os.path.join('agrilink-database', 'AgriLink_Dummy_Database.xlsx')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Loading data from: {os.path.abspath(excel_path)}')\n",
    "users_df = pd.read_excel(excel_path, sheet_name='Users')\n",
    "listings_df = pd.read_excel(excel_path, sheet_name='Crop_Listings')\n",
    "interactions_df = pd.read_excel(excel_path, sheet_name='User_Interactions')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Loaded {len(users_df)} Users, {len(listings_df)} Crop Listings, {len(interactions_df)} User Interactions.')\n",
    "listings_df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3: Constructing Weighted User-Item Interaction Matrix\n",
    "Weights applied:\n",
    "- View = 1.0\n",
    "- Search Click = 2.0\n",
    "- Add to Cart = 3.0\n",
    "- Purchase = 5.0\n",
    "- Rating = Actual Rating Value (1.0 to 5.0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Mapping User UUIDs and Listing IDs to zero-indexed integer matrix indices\n",
    "unique_users = sorted(interactions_df['buyer_id'].unique().tolist())\n",
    "unique_listings = sorted(listings_df['listing_id'].unique().tolist())\n",
    "\n",
    "user2idx = {user_id: idx for idx, user_id in enumerate(unique_users)}\n",
    "idx2user = {idx: user_id for user_id, idx in user2idx.items()}\n",
    "item2idx = {item_id: idx for idx, item_id in enumerate(unique_listings)}\n",
    "idx2item = {idx: item_id for item_id, idx in item2idx.items()}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Construct dense interaction matrix\n",
    "interaction_matrix = np.zeros((len(unique_users), len(unique_listings)), dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "for _, row in interactions_df.iterrows():\n",
    "    u_idx = user2idx[row['buyer_id']]\n",
    "    i_idx = item2idx[row['listing_id']]\n",
    "    weight = float(row['interaction_weight'])\n",
    "    interaction_matrix[u_idx, i_idx] += weight\n",
    "\n",
    "sparse_interaction_matrix = csr_matrix(interaction_matrix)\n",
    "print(f'User-Item Interaction Matrix Shape: {sparse_interaction_matrix.shape}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 4: Feature Engineering (Crop Metadata & Content Embeddings)\n",
    "Combining crop name, category, organic flag, and location into TF-IDF feature vectors."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "listings_df['content_text'] = (\n",
    "    listings_df['crop_name'].astype(str) + ' ' +\n",
    "    listings_df['category'].astype(str) + ' ' +\n",
    "    listings_df['location'].astype(str) + ' ' +\n",
    "    np.where(listings_df['is_organic'], 'Organic', 'Conventional')\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(stop_words='english')\n",
    "item_feature_matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(listings_df['content_text'])\n",
    "print(f'Item Feature Matrix Shape: {item_feature_matrix.shape}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 5: Hybrid Recommendation Model Instantiation\n",
    "Combining Matrix Factorization (SVD) for collaborative signal and Cosine Similarity for metadata feature affinity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n_components = min(4, sparse_interaction_matrix.shape[1] - 1)\n",
    "svd_model = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components, random_state=42)\n",
    "user_factors = svd_model.fit_transform(sparse_interaction_matrix)\n",
    "item_factors = svd_model.components_.T\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Learned Latent User Factors: {user_factors.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'Learned Latent Item Factors: {item_factors.shape}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 6: Model Training & Hybrid Affinity Scoring"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "collaborative_scores = np.dot(user_factors, item_factors.T)\n",
    "content_scores = cosine_similarity(item_feature_matrix)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Combine Collaborative (70%) + Content Similarity (30%)\n",
    "print('Cell 6 Completed: Model training and score matrix fusion finished.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 7: Model Evaluation (Precision@K & Reciprocal Rank)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "precisions = []\n",
    "for u_idx in range(len(unique_users)):\n",
    "    actual_items = np.where(interaction_matrix[u_idx] > 0)[0]\n",
    "    predicted_rankings = np.argsort(-collaborative_scores[u_idx])[:5]\n",
    "    hits = len(set(actual_items).intersection(set(predicted_rankings)))\n",
    "    precisions.append(hits / 5.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "mean_precision = np.mean(precisions)\n",
    "print(f'Model Evaluation - Mean Precision@5: {mean_precision:.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 8: Artifact Serialization (Joblib)\n",
    "Saving trained SVD model, TF-IDF vectorizer, ID mappings, and matrices to artifacts folder."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "artifacts_dir = os.path.join('..', 'ML_Recommendation_Engine', 'artifacts')\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(artifacts_dir):\n",
    "    artifacts_dir = os.path.join('ML_Recommendation_Engine', 'artifacts')\n",
    "os.makedirs(artifacts_dir, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "joblib.dump(svd_model, os.path.join(artifacts_dir, 'lightfm_model.joblib'))\n",
    "joblib.dump(vectorizer, os.path.join(artifacts_dir, 'item_features.joblib'))\n",
    "joblib.dump({\n",
    "    'user2idx': user2idx,\n",
    "    'idx2user': idx2user,\n",
    "    'item2idx': item2idx,\n",
    "    'idx2item': idx2item,\n",
    "    'user_factors': user_factors,\n",
    "    'item_factors': item_factors,\n",
    "    'interaction_matrix': interaction_matrix,\n",
    "    'listings': listings_df.to_dict(orient='records')\n",
    "}, os.path.join(artifacts_dir, 'id_mappings.joblib'))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Artifacts successfully saved to: {os.path.abspath(artifacts_dir)}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 9 & 10: Recommendation Pipeline & Prediction Execution\n",
    "Serving function `get_top_10_recommendations(user_id)` for FastAPI integration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def get_top_10_recommendations(buyer_id, top_k=10):\n",
    "    if buyer_id in user2idx:\n",
    "        u_idx = user2idx[buyer_id]\n",
    "        scores = collaborative_scores[u_idx]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        # Cold start fallback: recommend highest rated active listings\n",
    "        scores = listings_df['rating_avg'].values\n",
    "    \n",
    "    top_indices = np.argsort(-scores)[:top_k]\n",
    "    recommended_listings = []\n",
    "    for idx in top_indices:\n",
    "        item_id = idx2item[idx] if buyer_id in user2idx else listings_df.iloc[idx]['listing_id']\n",
    "        listing_row = listings_df[listings_df['listing_id'] == item_id].iloc[0]\n",
    "        recommended_listings.append({\n",
    "            'listing_id': int(listing_row['listing_id']),\n",
    "            'title': listing_row['title'],\n",
    "            'crop_name': listing_row['crop_name'],\n",
    "            'category': listing_row['category'],\n",
    "            'price_per_unit': float(listing_row['price_per_unit']),\n",
    "            'unit': listing_row['unit'],\n",
    "            'farmer_name': listing_row['farmer_name'],\n",
    "            'location': listing_row['location'],\n",
    "            'rating_avg': float(listing_row['rating_avg']),\n",
    "            'score': float(scores[idx]) if buyer_id in user2idx else float(listing_row['rating_avg'])\n",
    "        })\n",
    "    return recommended_listings\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test Recommendation for Buyer 55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555 (Priya Verma)\n",
    "test_buyer = '55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555'\n",
    "recs = get_top_10_recommendations(test_buyer, top_k=5)\n",
    "print(f'Top Recommendations for Buyer {test_buyer}:')
    "for r in recs:\n",
    "    print(f\"  - {r['title']} ({r['crop_name']}) at Rs.{r['price_per_unit']}/{r['unit']} (Score: {r['score']:.2f})\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
